pure python/scipy implementations. 'measured' = wall-clock of these implementations; 'model' = counts x building-block times with the Jacobian assembly charged at 2 mismatch evaluations (compiled-code-like), which strips python overhead from full Newton and favours the classical baseline.
base factorization per load scenario, measured (Jacobian derivatives + LU for chord; B', B'' LUs for fdlf): chord 0.655 ms, fdlf 0.477 ms; amortised over 22.0 contingencies per load scenario in this set, or over 240 for an exhaustive N-1 sweep
building blocks, median ms on one IEEE 118 problem (single thread): mismatch eval 0.0058; Jacobian assembly (acpf.jacobian) 0.5277; LU factorization of J (splu) 0.0530; triangular-solve pair with J factors 0.0050; spsolve(J, -F) (factorize+solve, as in NR) 0.0639; LU factorization of B' (splu) 0.0333; LU factorization of B'' (splu) 0.0138; triangular-solve pair with B' 0.0050; triangular-solve pair with B'' 0.0041; apply_dx (voltage update) 0.0077
